<title>USA: San Francisco $23 mln agency bond deal postponed.</title>
<headline>San Francisco $23 mln agency bond deal postponed.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The San Francisco Redevelopment Financing Authority postponed a $23.5 million revenue refunding bond deal originally scheduled for competitive pricing Wednesday, a market source said.</p>
<p>The deal was to sell at 1200 EST.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
